item.description:


            If your .NET pods are each using 1–2 GB of RAM, you may be leaving a lot of pod density — and money — on the table. Here are the first things I would look at.
Set Realistic Kubernetes Memory Limits Do not let every pod believe it has access to the whole node. 1 2 3 4 5 6 7
resources: requests: memory: &quot;512Mi&quot; cpu: &quot;100m&quot; limits: memory: &quot;768Mi&quot; cpu: &quot;1000m&quot;
